-- title:
--   Unique factorisation A=μ·{cⱼ}· H and sum re-indexing
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a commutative group and let $\mu, F, A, H$ be subgroups of $G$ with $\mu$ finite as a subset of $G$, subject to: every element of $\mu$ that also lies in $F$ equals $1$; $\mu \le A$; every $u \in A$ can be written $u = \zeta\varphi$ with $\zeta \in \mu$ and $\varphi \in F$; and $H \le F$, $H \le A$. Let $m \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to G$ be a family with $c_j \in F$ and $c_j \in A$ for all $j$, such that every $\varphi$ lying in both $F$ and $A$ satisfies $\varphi c_j^{-1} \in H$ for exactly one index $j$. The conclusion is a conjunction. First, for every $u \in A$ there is exactly one triple $(\zeta, j, h) \in \mu \times \mathrm{Fin}\,m \times H$ with $u = \zeta\, c_j\, h$. Second, for every additive commutative monoid $M$ and every $g : G \to M$ whose support meets $A$ in a finite set, $$\sum_{u \in A}^{\mathrm{f}} g(u) = \sum_{\zeta \in \mu} \sum_{j : \mathrm{Fin}\,m} \sum_{h \in H}^{\mathrm{f}} g(\zeta\, c_j\, h),$$ the outer sum being a finite sum over the finite set $\mu$ and the inner sums over $A$ and over $H$ being unconditional sums of finitely supported families.
--
--   This is the elementary coset bookkeeping behind a decomposition $A = \mu \cdot \bigsqcup_j c_j H$: the hypotheses encode that $A$ is generated by the finite group $\mu$ and the part of $F$ inside $A$, that $\mu$ meets $F$ trivially, and that the $c_j$ represent the $H$-cosets in $F \cap A$; the conclusion is the resulting bijection $\mu \times \mathrm{Fin}\,m \times H \to A$ together with the change of variables it induces on sums. It is used in the analytic work on units of a number field, where it re-indexes a sum over a group of units by torsion, coset representatives cut out by local and sign conditions, and a residual subgroup.
